      "content": "The consensus among major platforms is clear: content that relies on stereotypes to mock a politician is almost always removed as hate speech, regardless of its satirical framing. Platforms prioritize avoiding the amplification of anti-ethnic and anti-religious bias because the existence of the stereotype itself is the primary factor in their judgment. This approach is increasingly enforced by human moderators to prevent the \"spicy\" content loophole from being used to spread harmful generalizations about specific groups.\n\nRelying on this \"no loose end\" strategy is the safest path to avoid the specific \"de minimis\" liability (the \"not enough to matter\" defense) you are looking for. If your guidelines defend this stance against the \"it was just a joke\" argument you'll likely receive from creators, it ensures you align with the trend where political opinions are fair game, but group targeting is not.",
